  "summary": "Opulently decorated farmhouse interiors in Hälsingland, Sweden, featuring extensive painted surfaces, stenciling, and wallpaper.",
  "description": "Features richly painted ceilings, floral stencils, imported wallpapers, and elaborately decorated furniture; developed by wealthy farming families to display prosperity and social status. The interiors represent a fusion of folk art with European high design influences.",
  "culturalContext": "Hälsingland's decorated farmhouse interiors (UNESCO, seven farms) — 19th-century Swedish timber wealth — painted whole rooms for weddings and identity: stencil-and-stencil marbling (imitating wallpaper and stone), biblical and pastoral scenes by itinerant painters (dalkullor painters), ten+ decorated rooms per farm including unused \"status chambers\". The farms' stenciled profiles (Bortom Åa, Gästgivars) are Sweden's most complete vernacular interiors, and painted-farm restoration supports a living craft school.",
